@* Spec section 8.2: the template declares placement, and everything else is looked up at render
   time. A zone that resolved to no renderer emits nothing at all — no wrapper, no marker — so a
   template's own markup decides what an empty zone looks like.

   A zone that did resolve is rendered inside a boundary. It is the outer of the two levels: block
   lists put a second boundary around each block, so the usual failure is isolated to one block and
   this one catches what is left — a value-shaped renderer, or the block list renderer itself
   (spec section 15.3). *@
@if (RendererType is not null)
{
    <CmsErrorBoundary ZoneKey="@Name" Scope="CmsRenderScope.Zone">
        <DynamicComponent Type="RendererType" Parameters="RendererParameters" />
    </CmsErrorBoundary>
}
